WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:04.040
Let's go over a bunch of the more curious parts of "The Old Hunters".

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:07.100
Some of this Insights are pretty significant

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.900
and some are just minor observations but,

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.360
fact is, there's roughly fifty Insights in this video

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.740
so, make sure you keep an eye on that frenzy meter, yeah?

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:19.840
Let's start with the "Eye of a Blood-drunk Hunter"

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.400
in the same way that the Tonsil Stone allows

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.940
one Amygdala to transport us to the Nightmare Frontier,

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:30.580
the Eye allows another Amygdala to transport us to the Hunter's Nightmare.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.440
I thought it was interesting to discover that

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.840
the Amygdala needs something related to

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.840
the corresponding Nightmare realm to transport us there.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.880
Next, the grave that connects the Hunter's Dream

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.640
to the Hunter's Nightmare is also the grave we find

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.420
the Old Hunter's Bone at in the Waking World.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.360
The "Old Hunter's Bone" allows a hunter to learn

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:52.000
the lost art of quickening,

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.240
which was a technique particular to the First Hunters.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:59.580
And, indeed, many hunters like Maria dash like this

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:00.860
in the Hunter's Nightmare

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.400
without use of the bone.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:06.460
Third, there's a deceased Amygdala in the Nightmare,

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:09.240
and as we discover this new realm,

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:14.480
we learn that nightmare realms are almost certainly linked to one another:

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:17.740
they all have Amygdala, they all have Winter Lanterns,

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:20.280
which are based of the doll in our dream.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.580
The ship masts in the Fishing Hamlet

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:24.800
can be seen from the Nightmare Frontier

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:28.040
and, you know, even the washed-up corpse of Kos

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:32.140
looks kind of similar to these things in the Nightmare Frontier.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:35.820
While learning more and more about this nightmare realms,

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:38.900
specially how they have a very real ability

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:41.800
to shape events in the Waking World.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:42.980
Next up,

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:45.620
have you noticed that the old hunters all wear a garb

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:48.260
with the same red cloth on the inside?

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:49.180
Maria, Gehrman, ...

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:53.020
their attire is consistent with the time that they're from

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:56.060
which, I thought, was a nice, subtle design touch.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.440
The description of the old hunter's gear

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.860
also tells us that the people in this time

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:01.980
were quite superstitious.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:02.980
For instance,

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:06.740
they used to think that the "beast blood crept up the right leg"

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:09.580
hence, they put a belt around the right trouser leg.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:12.380
As pointed out by a bunch of you in the first video,

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:16.320
thist might explain why Gehrman has a pegleg on his right.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:22.160
Some of you suggested that it might have been amputated in some outdated method of prevention.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.380
And Gehrman and his pegleg,

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:27.100
both are viewable in the trailer for the Old Hunters.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:28.200
Have a look here,

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.340
you can just see his pegleg

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:32.820
which is curious because it doesn't just make it

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.820
any old hunter wearing Gehrman's garb.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:38.960
it's Gehrman himself walking through the Fishing Hamlet here.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.760
It places Gehrman's character undeniably within the events

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.760
that the "Old Hunters" depicts.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:47.480
And we'll go into a bit more depth on that later.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.020
For now, though

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.740
look at the "blood lickers" you come across in the blood river.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:55.120
I used to think that blood lickers were limited to Cainhurst

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.180
as if there was some sort of strain of the old blood

00:02:58.180 --> 00:02:59.200
that created them,

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.240
because they're so different to other beasts.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:04.380
But, because they're here, it makes it more likely

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:08.540
that blood lickers just appear where a lot of blood has to be present.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.920
The blood lickers in Cainhurst, for example,

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:14.280
they likely appeared when the big slaughter took place there;

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:17.760
where the executioners wiped out all of the Vilebloods

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:18.900
and slaughtered them.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:23.040
This blood lickers would have fed on the corpses but, you know,

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.600
years have passed since then,

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.200
so all the blood lickers there are skinny

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.200
and roaming for food when we encounter them.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:33.420
But, the ones here in the nightmare in the blood river

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:34.960
are fat and bloated.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:41.960
In the "Old Hunters, there is a heavy concentration of items and NPC's related to the powder kegs:

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:43.320
the Gatling Gun,

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.540
the Piercing Rifle,

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:45.560
the Boom Hammer.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:48.240
All of there are weapons that the old hunters use

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:50.460
and all of it is going to help a lot

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:52.040
when we're putting together

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.460
a timeline for the things that we see in this nightmare.

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:56.540
Take Laurence, for example.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:59.660
The fact that he appears in the nightmare on fire

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:01.980
might be because this is how he died.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:04.600
Maybe he died to the Molotovs of the Powder Kegs,

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:07.180
maybe in the purge of Old Yharnam, perhaps.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.040
Just speculation, of course.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:12.400
The Gatling Gun hunter who we find in the cave

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:17.480
is described by his weapon as being the youngest of Djura's three companions.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:23.780
And he's wielding a portable version of the Gatling Gun that Djura operates in Old Yharnam.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.860
Given his relationship to Djura,

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:30.640
I find it really curious that, he too, seems to be protecting the beast.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:35.660
Why else would he be standing at the entrance to the dead end cave

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:39.800
with his back turned to four or five deadly beasts

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:41.740
hiding in the cave behind him?

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:47.280
And we see this behavior in the Saw Spear hunter of Old Yharnam as well.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:51.280
Who, I feel pretty comfortable now, calling one of Djura's companions.

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:54.700
When you reach Simon outside the first shortcut,

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:56.620
you can actually just kill him here

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:59.400
if you want his Bowblade weapon as soon as possible.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.100
And don't worry about the key he gives you later,

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:05.360
it will appear in the spot that he usually gives it to you.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:08.700
Another NPC I shoud mention is Valtr.

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:13.680
If you crush five vermin and reload the area to acquire his helmet,

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:18.360
his name and appearance will change to reflect that when you summon him.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:21.080
He becomes a helmetless Valtr,

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.380
the Beast Eater.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:25.860
His duties, apparently, have been passed down to you.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:31.560
In addition, your League stance also changes to have you place your hand in front of your heart.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:34.480
Before we start talking about Ludwig,

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:38.240
do you remember this snail girl that fell from the sky?

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:43.980
I'm sure a lot of you put together that she fell from the above water world above our heads

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:46.720
that's not able to be seen from this perspective.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.840
And I event got a shot of her falling from a distance

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.200
just to make sure that's where she's coming from.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:56.140
Someone pointed me to this video recorded by a Reddit user:

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:57.960
"Dr. Xanthine MD"

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:03.760
who discovered that you can actually revive this snail girl using the Madaras Wistle on her corpse.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.740
It must activate a part of the hitbox that's untouchable or someting,

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:09.400
because you can't damage her otherwise.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:11.400
Now, onto Ludwig.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.760
how many of you had this little blood corpse

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:15.080
survive the fight?

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:17.840
It's surprisingly difficult to keep him alive

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:20.500
and altogether pointless, really.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:23.800
He just chuckles to himself once the fight is over.

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:25.860
And if you look closely at Ludwig,

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.500
you do realize a few things;

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:30.900
he has eyes on the inside of his little growth here

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:34.960
and he's also wearing what looks to be the executioners' garb.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:39.460
And his Moonlight Greatsword is strapped to his back during phase one.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:43.240
It's really cool to see that he retains a bit of his humanity

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:45.200
when he lays eyes upon it.

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:49.960
If you leave Ludwig's head alive after talking to it and reload your game,

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:52.900
you'll reapear to find that Simon

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:55.360
put Ludwig out of his misery instead.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:57.400
There's an arrow through his eye.

00:06:57.460 --> 00:07:01.900
A couple of you guys in the first video pointed this out to me and I thought it was really cool.

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:05.660
But it was only after I watched "A German Spy" 's playthrough

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:09.340
that I figured out how to get the most dialogue out of these characters

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:12.080
and you know that's interesting information for me

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:14.200
since I need to record this dialogue.

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:16.960
You should check out "A German Spy" 's playthrough, by the way.

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:21.280
He's got like one of the most knowledgeable playthroughs of the DLC out there

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:25.300
and he uses some pretty overpowered techniques.

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:26.760
Moving on past Ludwig,

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:31.580
did you know that if you die outside the bell ringer's room, then he'll say this:

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:36.320
"Unending death awaits those who pry into the unknown."

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:39.380
Up ahead, in the main cathedral chamber

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:42.740
we discover that the all popular "how to pick up fair maidens"

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:45.620
has been ordered in bulk by the folks in the nightmare.

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:48.740
Must have been recommended by Gehrman, or something.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.520
One of these fair maidens here, is dressed in white

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:55.180
and recites the same phrases that Vicar Amelia did.

00:07:55.180 --> 00:07:57.180
Logically, this is Amelia.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:00.960
And, logically, she entered the nightmare after we killed her.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:03.360
She prays in a different location now,

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:07.160
but she's still potentially praying at Lawrence's skull.

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:09.660
Send the elevator up without you on it,

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:15.380
go underneath and you'll find Lawrence's human skull and the Church Cannon.

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:18.160
One of the coolest little details on the elevator

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:20.180
is the surgery altar itself.

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:22.960
Putting aside all of the symbolism involved

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:25.860
when we insert eyes into the inside of the skull

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:28.440
and ascend into the heavens.

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:32.720
How many of you actually noticed that there is a beast underneath the table?

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:35.940
I caught onto this when I read a tweet by "Hellkite Drake",

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.980
another uploader who you should check out.

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:40.920
The beast under the table reminded  him of the beast

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:43.340
in the opening cutscene of Bloodborne

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:45.220
when you get the blood transfusion.

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:46.920
And I got to agree.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.480
The whole scene here symbolizes, to me,

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:53.980
that "latent beasthood is always a threat lying in wait".

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:57.180
But it's also something that the Church awakened

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:58.400
through their experiments.

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:02.060
Worth noting also is the book, the bell,

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:06.560
and this hat-mask thing that looks curiously like Willem's.

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:08.760
Moving up to the Research Hall,

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:10.600
let's take a look at these statues.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:16.040
it's getting to the point now where we can sort of notice this trends in Bloodborne's architecture.

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:19.700
And I'm starting to see these hunched over shapes everywhere:

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.220
these things in the fishing village,

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:24.320
the fish-men in the village,

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:26.620
the alien statues in the Cathedral, ...

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:29.420
They really like this shape in Bloodborne.

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:32.080
When we finally finish Adeline's questline

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:34.860
she shares the Milkweed rune with us.

00:09:35.060 --> 00:09:41.920
On the Fextralife Wiki, someone has written that the inscription of the rune resembles the letters "H", "P"

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:45.200
which could be a reference to H. P. Lovecraft

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:48.480
whose work is clearly an inspiration for Bloodborne.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:52.340
In fact, the story of the Fishing Hamlet is incredibly similar

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:56.180
to Lovecraft's horror novel: The Shadows over Innsmouth,

00:09:56.180 --> 00:10:01.100
which a lot of people have pointed out to me in the third video's comment section.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:04.000
The plot details a secretive town,

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:05.600
humanoid fish-men,

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:08.100
and the notion of human sacrifice.

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:09.740
So, pretty similar.

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:13.600
But speaking of great bodies of water in the fishing village,

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:16.560
as pointed out by commenter "...",

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:22.480
the word "lock" from Lockshield means "lake" in Irish or Gaelic:

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:27.900
And, of course, this is all behind the giant ClockTower that Maria guards

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:31.680
In an earlier video,we pointed out that the hands aligned

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:33.360
to point to the great lake room.

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:34.140
But

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:36.140
what about the other rooms, here?

00:10:36.140 --> 00:10:37.560
Well, there are a bunch of the

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:38.980
and some are missing,

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:39.600
most of their.

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:42.680
But there is one here that I don't recognize;

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:44.960
It's this massive squiggles

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:48.720
and there's not another rune in the game like this, right?

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:51.900
The closest thing I can find are the "clockwise" runes

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:54.140
but even they don't have theses shapes.

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:59.340
And it's weird because 'Fromsoft' had a bunch of of runes they could have used here,

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:04.020
they didn't use all of them so, why put one here that doesn't exist in the game?

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:06.800
It's just making me curious, thinking like

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:09.040
there's something we haven't found yet.

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:15.400
And I should take this moment to pint out that no one has found the level 3 "guidance rune" yet.

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:21.780
The official DLC guide does tell us that it exists within the depth 5 Root Chalice dungeos,

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:25.320
so, if you're one of the rare, rare people who enjoy

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:29.460
doing the Chalice Dungeons, then get out there and find that rune.

